\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns YES if the receiver and \i anObject\i0  are equal, NO otherwise.  This method defines what it means for an instance to be equal.  For example, a container object might define two containers as equal if their corresponding objects all respond YES to an \b isEqual:\b0  request.  See the NSData, NSDictionary, NSArray, and NSString class specifications for examples of the use of this method.\
