\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(id)\b performSelector:\b0 (SEL)\i aSelector\i0  \b withObject:\b0 (id)\i anObject\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Sends an \i aSelector\i0  message to the receiver with \i anObject\i0  as the argument.  If \i aSelector\i0  is NULL, an NSInvalidArgumentException is raised.\
\fs14\
\fs28 This method is the same as \b performSelector:\b0  except that you can supply an argument for  \i aSelector\i0 .  \i aSelector\i0  should identify a method that takes a single argument of type \b id\b0 . For methods with other argument types and return values, use NSInvocation.\
\fs14\
\pard \s58 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28  \f3 -\f1 \'80\b performSelector:withObject:withObject:\b0 , \f3 -\f1 \'80\b methodForSelector:\b0  (NSObject class)\
